01:06:30.160 --> 01:06:34.260
And so the fact that it stands above a game that's currently on the Essential Games list

01:06:34.260 --> 01:06:36.820
is, like, that's one thumbs up.

01:06:36.820 --> 01:06:39.000
The other thumbs up is, does the game hold up today?

01:06:39.160 --> 01:06:42.280
And I really feel like that part's even more true, right?

01:06:42.340 --> 01:06:45.220
Forget about, is this, like, one of the best NES games?

01:06:45.300 --> 01:06:48.660
I just feel like this was a game that I never thought while I was playing it.

01:06:48.740 --> 01:06:51.060
Like, yeah, this is an NES game, all right.

01:06:51.180 --> 01:06:53.840
Like, if anything, it felt beyond that.

01:06:53.980 --> 01:07:03.380
It really does surprise me, not just graphically, not just with its size or variety.

01:07:03.380 --> 01:07:08.340
It really just surprises me in terms of what we've seen so far

01:07:08.340 --> 01:07:10.180
and what I think we're going to continue to see.

01:07:10.320 --> 01:07:14.200
I think Crystallis is one of those ones that just, you know,

01:07:14.320 --> 01:07:16.320
we're not going to see another one like it.

01:07:16.380 --> 01:07:19.460
And if we do, I will be very surprised.

01:07:19.660 --> 01:07:22.860
So for that reason, I'm putting Crystallis on the Essential Games list.

01:07:23.180 --> 01:07:25.360
Sean? Yeah, no notes.

01:07:27.080 --> 01:07:30.660
Pretty good, pretty good Essential Games list vote, Mike.

01:07:30.660 --> 01:07:32.060
Thank you.

01:07:32.620 --> 01:07:37.000
I will say that I think I might have also voted for Willow,

01:07:37.140 --> 01:07:40.060
but maybe who's to say?

01:07:40.240 --> 01:07:42.140
Like, I can't remember what I had for dinner yesterday.

01:07:43.600 --> 01:07:47.240
But yeah, this game is just so polished,

01:07:47.580 --> 01:07:53.860
and there's so much, like, there's more depth than we're used to,

01:07:53.860 --> 01:07:58.800
and the, like, just the reactivity of the world,

01:07:58.840 --> 01:08:01.680
like we were describing, like, in these certain towns,

01:08:01.880 --> 01:08:03.760
and, like, you know, you'll go back to a town,

01:08:03.860 --> 01:08:04.940
and, like, oh, everybody's kidnapped.

01:08:05.100 --> 01:08:08.400
Like, how'd that happen? They're supposed to just be stagnant

01:08:08.400 --> 01:08:10.920
and always saying the same line every time I talk to them.

01:08:10.920 --> 01:08:15.520
Like, the story is great for the time,

01:08:15.640 --> 01:08:18.120
and the gameplay is great regardless,

01:08:18.540 --> 01:08:22.900
and, again, I'm not a fan of grinding,

01:08:23.140 --> 01:08:24.580
but grinding's still a thing.

01:08:24.880 --> 01:08:28.120
So, yeah, this is an essential game for me as well.

01:08:29.120 --> 01:08:30.620
All right, that means it's in,

01:08:30.700 --> 01:08:32.640
but we need to hear from Joe.

01:08:33.000 --> 01:08:35.980
Yeah, the first thing that I noticed about this game

01:08:35.980 --> 01:08:37.580
was how good it feels to play.

01:08:38.260 --> 01:08:40.820
It does feel, I agree,

01:08:40.960 --> 01:08:43.860
it does feel kind of beyond what you would expect

01:08:43.860 --> 01:08:45.320
from an NES game.

01:08:45.620 --> 01:08:48.080
And then building on that, like I said,

01:08:48.180 --> 01:08:50.380
the design of the world,

01:08:50.520 --> 01:08:52.260
the design of the quest you're on

01:08:52.260 --> 01:08:54.140
gives you a lot more agency,

01:08:54.660 --> 01:08:56.280
and it feels a lot more modern

01:08:56.280 --> 01:08:59.020
in the sense that you don't have to be looking at a guide.

01:08:59.120 --> 01:09:01.840
You don't have a ton of bullshit that you have to get through.

01:09:02.100 --> 01:09:03.280
I won't say that there's none,

01:09:03.460 --> 01:09:07.440
but there, this game, I love this game.

01:09:07.580 --> 01:09:11.140
It was fantastic. It's definitely my style of game,

01:09:11.240 --> 01:09:12.960
so maybe that was working for it from the beginning,

01:09:13.060 --> 01:09:14.440
but I think even outside of that,

01:09:15.460 --> 01:09:17.640
this was a game that I enjoyed playing

01:09:17.640 --> 01:09:19.200
and want to keep playing.

01:09:19.360 --> 01:09:22.100
So I'm definitely going to vote this essential.

01:09:23.320 --> 01:09:24.720
All right, unanimous.

01:09:24.820 --> 01:09:25.800
You'll love to see it.

01:09:25.880 --> 01:09:27.840
I think that's the first time in a long time.

01:09:28.060 --> 01:09:29.600
That might be the first unanimous

01:09:29.600 --> 01:09:31.380
since Super Mario Bros.

01:09:31.620 --> 01:09:35.880
3 recorded back on June 2nd, 2023.

01:09:37.100 --> 01:09:39.220
So we found a way, guys.

01:09:39.400 --> 01:09:41.720
It took us a whole year and some more

01:09:41.720 --> 01:09:43.360
to agree on something,

01:09:43.380 --> 01:09:46.220
but we can all agree that this is essential.

01:09:46.460 --> 01:09:48.260
Although Joe never played Terra Cresta,

01:09:48.880 --> 01:09:51.080
so maybe he would have voted that essential.

01:09:51.080 --> 01:09:53.060
I gotta give it a try. And then Joe,

01:09:53.200 --> 01:09:55.380
did you vote Chippendale Rescue Rangers essential?

01:09:57.140 --> 01:09:58.640
I think so.

01:09:59.240 --> 01:10:00.220
I don't think I did.

01:10:00.900 --> 01:10:01.740
Okay, that's what it is.

01:10:01.740 --> 01:10:03.120
Because I remember being kind of reversed

01:10:03.120 --> 01:10:05.160
from the old DuckTales vote,

01:10:05.320 --> 01:10:07.220
or I didn't initially for some reason.

01:10:07.360 --> 01:10:11.220
Okay, so Mike and Joe voted essential on Chippendale,

01:10:12.040 --> 01:10:14.220
but Mike and Sean voted essential

01:10:14.220 --> 01:10:16.300
the very next episode for Dragon Spirit.

01:10:16.520 --> 01:10:18.420
That sounds right? You didn't vote for Dragon Spirit?

01:10:19.120 --> 01:10:20.200
Yeah, I think that's right.

01:10:20.400 --> 01:10:21.700
But I did vote for Willow also,

01:10:21.900 --> 01:10:23.220
so maybe all three of us voted for Willow.

01:10:23.240 --> 01:10:25.040
No, Sean did not vote for Willow.

01:10:25.280 --> 01:10:28.420
Whatever. I distinctly remember saying the words

01:10:28.420 --> 01:10:32.060
what a treat in my essential game.

01:10:32.160 --> 01:10:33.680
Go back, listeners, and look it up.

01:10:33.720 --> 01:10:34.600
I said what a treat.

01:10:35.560 --> 01:10:38.100
It was 20 episodes, but we got there.

01:10:38.740 --> 01:10:40.140
After a 20-episode drought,

01:10:40.400 --> 01:10:42.600
we have our newest essential game, Crystalis.

01:10:42.780 --> 01:10:44.700
Don't play the Game Boy Color version

01:10:46.160 --> 01:11:15.700
because you're always the chosen one listener. We'll see you next time.
